int i = m - 1;
int j = n - 1;
int k = m + n - 1;

while (i >= 0 && j >= 0) {
  if (a[i] > b[j]) a[k--] = a[i--];
  else a[k--] = b[j--];
}

// No sentinel loop needed for a because of in-place merge
while (j >= 0) a[k--] = b[j--];
```

After each iteration, `k` is the next output position, everything `> k` has been merged, and `a[0, i]` contains the unprocessed elements of `b`.

