unsigned i = m;
unsigned j = n;
unsigned k = m + n;

while (i > 0 && j > 0) {
  if (a[i - 1] > b[j - 1]) out[--k] = a[--i];
  else out[--k] = b[--j];
}

while (i > 0) out[--k] = a[--i];
while (j > 0) out[--k] = b[--j];
```

Comment:

- `i` = number of elements remaining in `a`
- `j` = number of elements remaining in `b`
- `k` = number of output slots remaining

